		(property "Design Note" "AZ431 bias resistor. (5.0 - 2.5)/1.5k = 1.67 mA nominal; at a -2% rail and the 2.510 V grade limit it is still 1.59 mA, comfortably over the 1.0 mA IKA minimum, and the ~27 uA drawn by the reference node is negligible beside it. Costs 1.67 mA on +5V_ANALOG, which is 17 mV more drop across R32 -- U3 still has ample headroom for 3.3 V out"
